<Layout title="Privacy - Your files stay local | KittySuite" description="How KittySuite handles local files, font downloads, browser storage and website requests."><article class="shell section tool-details"><h1>Your files stay yours.</h1><p>Images, PDFs, text, HTML and signatures selected in our tools are processed on your device. Our tools do not send that content to a processing server, analytics endpoint or model API.</p><h2>What the website requests</h2><p>Your browser downloads the website and, when needed, processing libraries, a font index and selected font files from this site's host. These requests do not include your file contents or typed text. Like any website host, the hosting provider can receive request metadata such as your IP address, browser information and requested asset path. We do not use ads or third-party trackers.</p><h2>Storage and permissions</h2><p>Your theme preference is stored in your browser. Fonts and site assets may be cached by the browser. Files are held in memory while a tool is open; reset or navigation releases working references. Downloads are saved where your browser chooses. Camera access is requested only when you choose to scan, and camera tracks stop when you finish or leave.</p><h2>Links and HTML</h2><p>Font source and licence links may open another site when you choose them. HTML tools remove scripts and external resources before rendering. They do not fetch URLs you paste. Browser extensions, the operating system and downloaded files are outside KittySuite's control.</p><h2>Limitations</h2><p>Local processing does not make every edit a security operation. Image blur is visual obfuscation. PDF crop hides edges without removing their underlying content. Redaction uses a separate raster rebuild workflow and discards the original PDF objects. Always review sensitive outputs before sharing.</p></article></Layout>
